From e3af2e58f6d3582e0475a7af17e67a914a27e148 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:24:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/78] Port the IFF85/ILBM reader and load the gothic font

Ports the Electronic Arts IFF85 reader compiled into the game: H098
buffered I/O, H086 group and chunk parser, H039 ChunkMoreBytes, H087
GetBMHD/GetCMAP/GetBODY, H088 ByteRun1 UnPackRow, H054 RowBytes, H099
MaxPackedSize and the H040 ILBM callbacks with Read_ILBM. Chunk headers
and BMHD are decoded from big-endian bytes, so the host reads them
correctly. H030+$0C10 now loads gothic.lbm through Open_ResourceFile and
hands it to H049+$0438.

tests/ilbm_test.c with scripts/check_ilbm.py (an independent decoder)
gives identical planes and colours for all seven .lbm files of the game.
Host paths that are absolute are no longer treated as game-relative.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
